        "topic": "Accounting Equation",
        "question_type": "Practical",
        "exam_year": "2007",
        "question_text": "<p>The assets of a business are \u20b5120,000 and the liabilities are \u20b540,000. What is the owner's equity?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Using the accounting equation: $Assets = Liabilities + Owner's\thinspace Equity$.<br>Rearranged to find owner's equity: $Owner's\thinspace Equity = Assets - Liabilities$.<br>Substitute the given values: $Owner's\thinspace Equity = \u20b5120,000 - \u20b540,000 = \u20b580,000$.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
