        "topic": "Bank Reconciliation",
        "question_type": "Practical",
        "exam_year": "2007",
        "question_text": "<p>The cash book balance of a business is \u20b515,000 (debit), while the bank statement shows a balance of \u20b518,000 (credit). The following were discovered:<br><i>Unpresented cheques: \u20b54,000</i><br><i>Bank charges not recorded: \u20b51,000</i><br><i>Deposit not yet credited: \u20b52,000</i><br>Calculate the adjusted cash book balance.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Start with the cash book balance: \u20b515,000.<br>Adjust for items not recorded in the cash book:<br><b>Add: Deposit not yet credited \u20b52,000</b><br><b>Less: Bank charges \u20b51,000</b><br>Adjusted cash book balance = \u20b515,000 + \u20b52,000 - \u20b51,000 = <b>\u20b516,000</b>.</p>",
